    "chunk_size_bytes": 2004,
    "chunk_text": "(iii)the Legal Draftsman or hisnominee not below the rankof a Senior Assistant LegalDraftsman; and\n\nReplacement ofsection 2 of Act,No. 3 of 1969.\n\n\u201cEstablishmentandconstitutionof the LawCommission.\n\nLaw Commission (Amendment)Act, No. 19 of 20162\n\n(2) The President shall appoint one of themembers of the Commission to be the Chairmanof the Commission.\n\n(3) An appointed member shall, unless heearlier vacates his office, hold office for suchperiod, not exceeding five years, as may bedetermined by the President at the time of hisappointment, and shall be eligible forreappointment:\n\nProvided, however, that if an appointedmember vacates his office prior to theexpiration of his term of office, his successorshall, unless he earlier vacates his office, holdoffice only for the unexpired portion of theterm of the member whom he succeeds.\n\n(4) An appointed member may resign fromhis office by writing under his hand addressedto the President.\n\n(5) There shall be paid to the members ofthe Commission for their services suchremuneration as may be determined by theMinister, with the prior concurrence of theMinister assigned the subject of Finance.\u201d.\n\n3Law Commission (Amendment)Act, No. 19 of 2016\n\n3.Section 8 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the substitution for the words \u201canyCommissioner\u201d of the words \u201cany member of theCommission\u201d.\n\n4.Section 11 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the substitution for the words \u201cThe PermanentSecretary to the Ministry\u201d of the words \u201cThe Secretary to theMinistry\u201d.\n\n5.Section 12 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the substitution for the words \u201ctheCommissioners\u201d of the words \u201cthe members of theCommission\u201d.\n\n6.Section 13 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the repeal of the definition of theexpression\u201cCommissioner\u201d.\n\n7.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAmendment ofsection 13 of theprincipalenactment."
  },
