    "chunk_text": "THERETO.\u201d. 3. Section 2 of the principal enactment is hereby amended by the repeal of subsection (2) thereof and the substitution therefor of the following subsection:- \u201c(2) The members of the Institute shall consist of Corporate and Non-Corporate members.\u2019\u2019.\n\nShort title.\n\nAmendment of the Long Title of Law, No. 33 of 1975.\n\nAmendment of section 2 of the principalenactment.\n\n4. The following new section is hereby inserted immediately after section 2 of the principal enactment and shall have effect as section 2A in the principal enactment:-\n\n2A. The grading of members of the Institute shall be as speci\ufb01 ed in Schedule A to this Act.\u201d.\n\n5. Section 5 of the principal enactment is hereby amended by the insertion immediately after paragraph (k) thereof, of the following new paragraphs:-\n\n\u201c(kk) to determine, from time to time, the valuation standards, as the Corporation may deem appropriate;\n\n(kkk) to determine a scheme of assessment of professional competence or any other requirement for continuous professional development;\u201d.\n\n6. Section 7 of the principal enactment is hereby repealed and the following section substituted therefor:-\n\n7. (1) Any person who satis\ufb01 es the quali\ufb01 cations and experience speci\ufb01 ed in Schedule B to this Act may apply for the membership of the Institute in such form and manner as provided in Schedule C to this Act.\n\n(2) Any person who has duly applied under subsection (1) may be enrolled as a member of the Institute on the payment of the prescribed entrance fee and membership fee.\u201d.\n\n\u201cGrading of members.\n\nInsertion of new section 2A in the principal enactment.\n\nAmendment of section 5 of the principal. enactment.\n\nAmendment of section 7 ofthe principalenactment.\u201cApplication for membership of the Institute.\n\n3 Institute of Valuers of Sri Lanka (Amendment)Act, No. 9 of 2019\n\n7. The following new sections are hereby inserted immediately after section 7 of the principal enactment and shall have effect as sections 7A, 7B, 7C and 7D in the principal enactment:-"
